# Neighbour summary

**Neighbour summary** is a future lens: a query that restates each card linked
from the current card in two sentences, written from the current card's point
of view. It would generate what the section "Neighbouring concepts" on every
card now holds by hand. It is a design and does not run on the current HQL;
this card must not be rendered.

## What it would do

Each concept card ends its account with short summaries of its neighbours. A
summary there is not a copy of the neighbour's definition. It says what the
neighbour is *as seen from here*: on the card for induction, deduction is "the
half of the cycle that gives a hypothesis something to be tested on". Written
by hand, these summaries go stale when the neighbour changes.

The lens gives an agent the description of the current card, the description
of the neighbour and the declared relation, and asks for the restatement. The
cell is cached, so the agent runs again only when one of the two cards
changes.

This is [[summarization]] under a constraint, and it is also the smallest case
of a card whose content depends on a reading of other cards. Once the
generated text is integrated and a later run reads it, the cycle of
[[render-integrate-execute]] is closed.

## The design

```hql
import future
import ai

summarizer = Agent(@[[summarizer]])
this
| uplinks
| filter(e => e.data.relation != none)
| map(e => {
    card: e.target,
    relation: e.data.relation,
    summary: summarizer | ask(
      Prompt("Restate {target} in two sentences for a reader of {source}, given that the relation is {relation}."),
      Context(source = this.sections["Description"], target = @[[e.target]].sections["Description"], relation = e.data.relation)
    )
  })
```

## What current HQL lacks

- `this`, and access to one section of a card.
- The `ai` module: an agent defined by a card, a prompt, a context, `ask`.
- `cached` cells, so that a generated summary is kept and not regenerated on
  every render.

## Relations

- It is an application of [[summarization]] {relation: uses} with a fixed point of view.
- Its generated text enters a card through [[render-integrate-execute]] {relation: uses}.
- It would be run by a [[reflective-agent]] {relation: uses} reading the vault it writes into.
- It serves the question [[ai-support-in-hql]] {relation: answers}.
